-- title:
--   Good points read places off the Igusa nodes (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$ (hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $(q : \overline{\mathbb Q})$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`). The finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ is required (`hW`) to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}) \in$ `ssJSet q`, where `ssJSet q K` is the set of those $j \in K$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $K$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point over $K$. The two Laurent-series fields in play are `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of level $q^2M'$ with character group `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; the hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   Reduction data. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the reduced field with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places, compatibility with $A$ and with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-scalars, the existence for each nonzero $f$ of a scalar $c$ with $c\cdot f$ integral of nonzero residue, preservation of degrees of places, and compatibility of order functions under `mapDomain` of the place map. The hypothesis `hR₀` pins this reduction down coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficients lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, viewed as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Igusa charts. $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and `OIg` assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each point of the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$. Four hypotheses constrain it: `hIg_inf` identifies `OIg (lineInfty q)` as the Gauss-type ring, $f$ belonging to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x, y$ with coefficients in $A$, the reduction of $y$ nonzero, with $f \cdot y = x$ after coefficientwise inclusion; `hIg` states that every $\ell$ is of the form $\mathrm{redQ}_q(\gamma)\cdot$`lineInfty q` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `OIg ℓ` the pullback of `OIg (lineInfty q)` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of `OIg`; and `hIg_perm` asserts that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family, i.e. equals `OIg ∘ σ` for some permutation $\sigma$ of the projective line.
--
--   Supersingular charts. `OSS` assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each $s \in W$, subject to: `hSS_A`, that an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `OSS s` exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is regular wherever the base-changed $j$-expansion is (precisely: $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the element given by `coeffEmb` applied to `jq`), if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OSS s`, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue the difference $f - a$ lies in `OSS s` and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that `OSS s` is its own pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that for each $s$ there is $t \in$ `OSS s` such that $t - a$ lies in `OSS s` and is a unit there for every $a \in A$.
--
--   Prolongation. $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2M') (levelH q M')`, that is, a valuation subring with a surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, and with the scalar-adjustment property; `hR` identifies $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with `OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O` states that $f$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OIg (lineInfty q)`.
--
--   Arithmetic of the base. $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and lies in $A$ (`hπ`, `hπP`). A subfield $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is given together with $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that the contraction of $A$ to $k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`). Further auxiliary data: a prime $\ell \ne q$ with $\ell \ge 3$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ whose elements are exactly those of $K_1$ lying in $A$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The assertion. Equip `fieldBar q M'` with the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of $k_0$ in `fieldBar q M'` satisfying four conditions: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is everything; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, linear independence of $c$ over $K'$ together with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose underlying Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of `coeffEmb`, belongs to $F_0$. Write $T_1$ for the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the image of $K_1$. Let $T_1$ carry an $A_1$-algebra structure for which the structure map sends $a \in A_1$ to the image of $a$ in `fieldBar q M'`, let $j_1 \in T_1$ have image in `fieldBar q M'` equal to the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by `coeffEmb` applied to `jq` (included via `hle`), with $j_1 \ne 0$, and let $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ be a finite set of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to that field such that every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ has image in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue $j(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$, and such that $Q \in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ holds exactly when there is $s \in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ is in the valuation subring of $Q$, for all $g$.
--
--   The statement then introduces, over the scheme $\mathfrak X_1 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the two integral chart algebras `chartAlgFin` (integral closure of $A_1[j_1]$ in $T_1$) and `chartAlgInf` (integral closure of $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), the following predicates. `InStalk x f`, for $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$: for every point $y$ of $\mathrm{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` whose image under `ιFin` is $x$ there are $g, h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for every point $y$ of $\mathrm{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` over $x$ with `chartAlgInf` in place of `chartAlgFin`. `InMax x f`: the same two clauses with the extra requirement $g \in y$. `Centred P x`, for a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: $P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies that the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ precisely when `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x`: the image of $x$ under `toBase` is the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; for every point $y$ of either chart over $x$, every chart element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ is not in `ssJSet q Ω`. `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2M') (levelH q M')` over the residue field of $A$: every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that residue is a non-unit there precisely when `InMax x f`. `OffBranch x`: for every line $\ell \ne$ `lineInfty q` and every point $y$ of either chart over $x$ there is a chart element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of `OIg ℓ` and which does not lie in $y$.
--
--   The conclusion is the single assertion that for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ satisfying `GoodPt x` and every place $Q$ with `Reads x Q`, one has $Q \notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. The abbreviations `Centred` and `OffBranch` are introduced in the statement but do not occur in this conclusion.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ instance of the step, on the Igusa leg of the semistable-covering argument, which shows that the place of the reduced level-$q^2M'$ function field read off at a good closed point of the two-chart integral model is none of the supersingular (Igusa node) places: a good point lies on the $\infty$-Igusa component and has non-supersingular $j$-invariant, so the place it reads cannot lie under a supersingular place of the level-$M'$ reduced field. It feeds the companion statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two), which upgrades this to uniqueness of the read place together with the off-branch property.
